body:
## [ISSUE] Federated (Mimir) rule groups lose their immutability guard in `useAllAlertRuleAbilities`

**Severity:** MEDIUM — Edit/Delete/Pause become available for federated rules that the ruler API does not allow users to modify this way.

### The Problem

Before:
```ts
const isFederated = isFederatedRuleGroup(rule.group);
```
After, `useAllAlertRuleAbilities(rule: CombinedRule)` just calls `useAllRulerRuleAbilities(rule.rulerRule, groupIdentifierV2)`, which has:
```ts
// TODO: Add support for federated rules
// const isFederated = isFederatedRuleGroup();
const isFederated = false;
```
`CombinedRule.group.source_tenants` is still available in the wrapper, but it is no longer passed down.

### Theory / Proof

`isFederatedRuleGroup` (`utils/rules.ts:373`) returns true when `source_tenants` is set. `immutableRule = isProvisioned || isFederated || isPluginProvided` drives `Update`, `Delete`, `Pause` and `Restore`. `useAlertRuleAbility` / `useAllAlertRuleAbilities` are still used by `components/rules/RuleActionsButtons.tsx:57` (Edit button in the legacy list), `RuleDetailsButtons.tsx` and `GrafanaRuleQueryViewer.tsx`, so for a Mimir group with `source_tenants` the Edit button now appears.

### What happens today vs. what will break

Federated groups used to be read-only in the UI. After this PR a user with `alert.rules.external:write` sees Edit/Delete on them. Saving through the editor rewrites the group without the `source_tenants` semantics the UI cannot represent, or the ruler rejects the request.

### Research

Mimir documents federated rule groups (`source_tenants`) as a special mode that the Grafana editor does not manage: https://grafana.com/docs/mimir/latest/references/architecture/components/ruler/#federated-rule-groups. The prom-based hook correctly notes that Grafana-managed rules cannot be federated. That argument does not apply to the CombinedRule path, which also covers data source rules.

### Recommendation

Keep the check in the CombinedRule wrapper by passing it through:

```ts
export function useAllAlertRuleAbilities(rule: CombinedRule): Abilities<AlertRuleAction> {
  const groupIdentifierV2 = useMemo(() => groupIdentifier.fromCombinedRule(rule), [rule]);
  return useAllRulerRuleAbilities(rule.rulerRule, groupIdentifierV2, { isFederated: isFederatedRuleGroup(rule.group) });
}
```

and use `options.isFederated ?? false` inside `useAllRulerRuleAbilities`.
